   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Full rated power holds up to 70 °C ambient; between 70 °C and 155 °C it drops linearly to nothing."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "0402 parts are unmarked. 0603 parts carry three characters: R as the decimal point (R10 is 100 mΩ), or for ±1% E96 values a two-digit index followed by Z (02Z is 102 mΩ). 0805, 1206, 1210, 1812, 2010 and 2512 parts carry four characters with R as the decimal point (R100 is 100 mΩ, R102 is 102 mΩ)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Reflow: rise at under 3 °C/s, preheat from 150 °C to 200 °C for 60 to 120 s; stay above 217 °C for 60 to 150 s with a 240 to 260 °C peak held at most 10 s; cool at under 6 °C/s. Wave: rise at under 3 °C/s to 120 °C, peak 250 to 260 °C for at most 10 s, cool at under 6 °C/s. Hand soldering: 350±10 °C iron for less than 3 s, tip off the body."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Environments that degrade performance",
   "page": 11,
   "text": "Performance may suffer in high heat; in sea air or corrosive gases such as Cl2, H2S, NH3, SO2 and NO2; when wetted by unverified water, oil, chemicals or organic solvents; when covered by unverified resin or paint; and when, after soldering, unclean flux is used or the parts are washed with water or water-soluble cleaners."
  }
 ],
